prompt.text:
Implement a new TypeScript module exporting `ReviewRecord`, `ReviewRow`, `ReviewPage`, and `buildReviewPage`.

Public API:

```ts
export interface ReviewRecord {
  readonly contributor: string;
  readonly document: string;
  readonly submittedOn: string;
  readonly score: number | null;
}
export interface ReviewRow extends ReviewRecord { readonly status: "pending" | "scored"; }
export interface ReviewPage {
  readonly title: "Pending Reviews";
  readonly rows: readonly ReviewRow[];
}
export function buildReviewPage(role: string, records: readonly ReviewRecord[]): ReviewPage;
```

Only the exact role `"reviewer"` is authorized; every other string, including different casing and whitespace variants, causes `Error` before record validation. Validate each record in input order: `contributor`, `document`, and `submittedOn` must each contain at least one non-whitespace character; otherwise throw `TypeError`. Scores must be null or finite numbers from 0 through 100 inclusive; otherwise throw `RangeError`.

Return rows sorted by ascending `submittedOn` using ordinary string comparison. Equal dates retain input order. Do not trim or otherwise normalize returned strings. A null score maps to `pending`; every numeric score, including zero, maps to `scored`. Empty input returns an empty fresh row array. Return a new page, new row array, and new row objects on every successful call. Never mutate or sort the input array, and returned rows must not alias input record objects.

